{
 "comment": "The values that really reach the fields of the signed config documents and of the bootstrap file, and where they are put in a document. Each entry sets the path of the base document of the schema (kits/conformance/config/schema-vectors.json) to the shape, with $v replaced by each value of the domain, and the schema must accept every one; an entry with `id` renames the one item of a keyed kind to the value. A domain is the characters a value may begin with and may go on with, and its shortest and longest length; the values are made from it in one way, shared by Go and Rust: for each first character, a value of the shortest and one of the longest length, the rest cycling through the characters of `rest` from the position of the first (so the first characters and the rest are all seen at both ends of the length range), minus `except`, plus `extra`. A domain with `values` holds the values themselves. A `refused` value must not validate. The class of bug this is for: the audit table took a key id only if it began with a letter or a digit, and one thumbprint in thirty-two begins with - or _ (#1610); a schema is never stricter than the loaders, and these are the values that prove it where the loaders are simple. Hand-written; Go and Rust must agree on every entry (REQ-DATA-038, REQ-OPS-002).",
 "domains": {
  "thumbprint": {
   "doc": "an RFC 7638 thumbprint of a key: SHA-256 in base64url without padding, 43 characters. One in thirty-two begins with - or _ (#1610), and the last character is one of 16 in a real one; the schema takes any 43 characters of the alphabet and key@ checks the canonical form",
   "first": "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_",
   "rest": "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_",
   "min": 43,
   "max": 43,
   "refused": [
    "",
    "has space",
    "aéaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa=",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa+"
   ]
  },
  "store_part": {
   "doc": "a boundary's tenant, or the id of an item of a keyed kind: a store part, 1 to 128 of a-z 0-9 - _ ., never . or .. (store-api.md Address encoding). The schema takes . and .. too: it is never stricter than the loaders",
   "first": "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_.",
   "rest": "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_.",
   "min": 1,
   "max": 128,
   "except": [
    ".",
    ".."
   ],
   "refused": [
    "has space",
    "UPPER",
    "aé",
    "a/b",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
   ]
  },
  "node": {
   "doc": "a node of the slot map: a store part of at most 64 characters, as key@ and the card driver name a node",
   "first": "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_.",
   "rest": "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_.",
   "min": 1,
   "max": 64,
   "except": [
    ".",
    ".."
   ],
   "refused": [
    "",
    "has space",
    "Node",
    "a/b",
    "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
   ]
  },
  "credential": {
   "doc": "the name of a credential in the secret source: letters and digits first, then letters, digits and - _ . up to 128 characters (systemd LoadCredential=). An empty name is none",
   "first": "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789",
   "rest": "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_.",
